{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Where the restart time goes (measured 2026-11-01, read-only)\n\n**Crash window, 2026-10-29 UTC (nginx logs on the box):** OOM kill 00:47:26.7. 00:47:27 the 10 in-flight `/mcp` requests end (`upstream prematurely closed`); one `connect() failed (111)`; then 00:47:28 / :30 / :35 / :43 / :45 / :53 all `recv() failed (104: Connection reset by peer)`, meaning the published port accepted but nothing listened inside the container. The next `/mcp*` request, 00:48:14, was answered by the app (404 on `/mcp/health`). The container's own log for that restart is gone (it logged to json-file then; journald since creatable-isleted-kusimanse).\n\n**Start-to-listen on the box, deploy of 2026-11-01 (container `rebar-mcp-e5a7e75b7fa7-8093`, journald):**\n\n| UTC | step |\n|---|---|\n| 08:57:12.54 | container started (`State.StartedAt`) |\n| 08:57:12.62 | entrypoint first line (provisioning forks to background) |\n| 08:57:15.28 to 08:57:35.07 | `PARENT_CHAIN_FORK_RESOLVED` warnings from the reducer, i.e. the in-process boot ensure sweep (`run_startup_store_sweep`) replaying tickets |\n| 08:57:36.93 | uvicorn `Started server process` |\n| 08:57:36.97 | startup handshake done, `Uvicorn running` (handshake 0.04 s) |\n| 08:57:38.66 | first `/health` 200 (autodeploy probe) |\n| 08:57:38.87 | nginx cutover |\n\nSo 24.4 s pass before the process listens, and the listener is serving 0.04 s after that. nginx health gating adds nothing on a crash restart: nginx stays pointed at the same port.\n\n**Phase timing, local, isolated copy of the tickets store (9,853 ticket dirs), `main()` steps timed individually, 2 runs:** import 0.29 / 0.17 s; boot ensure sweep 16.92 / 15.68 s; config 0.53 / 0.39 s; `build_server` 0.84 / 0.65 s. Inside the sweep, `snapshot-close-metadata` took 16.22 / 14.81 s; every other unit took 0.24 s or less.\n\n**Comparison:** dewy-rotatable-tarsier measured container start to uvicorn start at 5.20 / 7.54 / 5.49 s on 2026-08-28. The `snapshot-close-metadata` unit landed in 3835269d792 (2026-10-28 11:18 PDT), which is an ancestor of f8ddcaf88e6, the build running at the 10-29 crash. docs/migrations.md already records \"a converged sweep still costs about 21.5 s under the lock\" and lists MCP boot as a run site. The sweep runs synchronously in `main()` before `build_server`/`run_mcp`, so that cost lands directly in time-to-listen.\n\nOn the box the entrypoint also runs the full ensure registry in the background (`reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh`; it finished at 08:57:40.68, after bind), so the in-process boot sweep duplicates the registry run.\n\n## Claude Code reconnect limits\n\n- code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp: for a remote server that drops mid-session, Claude Code makes 5 attempts with exponential backoff starting at 1 s and doubling. In an interactive session it then marks the server failed and shows \"open /mcp to reconnect\". `/mcp reconnect all` needs v2.1.284 or later. In `claude -p` and Agent SDK sessions, after a transient error such as a 5xx, it keeps retrying in the background for up to about 30 minutes.\n- The documented env vars (code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars: `MCP_TIMEOUT`, `MCP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS`, `MCP_TOOL_TIMEOUT`, `CLAUDE_CODE_MCP_*`) include none that changes the reconnect count or backoff.\n- anthropics/claude-code#55228, \"hardcoded 5-attempt reconnect cap\", was closed as not planned (stale) on 2026-06-01. #101280, \"HTTP MCP client gives up after ~15 s of connection-refused\", has been open since 2026-10-11. A comment there reports that 2.1.299 headless added up to 8 background attempts after the ladder, while a desktop-hosted 2.1.299 session still gave up. The 10-29 session (2.1.308, interactive) logged \"Max reconnection attempts (5) reached, giving up\" with no background retry."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793525483367847001,"uuid":"9aeb9abe-a508-4680-8db5-facb1a5d2fc2"}